{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74-brief.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74h.md'","aggregated_output":"# Council round 74: review the slice-1 build design before any code (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n\n## What to review\n\n`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`, the build design for the first slice of the \"Forecast unavailable\"\nrelease. The governing documents:\n- `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4, ready per `codex-r72d.md`);\n- D726, D756, D757 and D758 at the end of `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`;\n- AGENTS.md §2 (design tables before code), §3 (one owner; the writer refuses), §4 (tests) and §5.\n\nCode that the design reuses:\n- `src/hivemind/service.py`: `resolve_bound`, `view_exists`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `evidence`, `evidence_record`,\n  `ladder_bands`;\n- `src/hivemind/bundle.py`: `read_snapshot`, `item_lookup`, `view_bundle`;\n- `src/hivemind/views/store.py`: `view_key`, `rungs_of`;\n- `src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10`;\n- `src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24`;\n- `src/hivemind/idea.py`, for the idea question.\n\n## Questions\n\n1. **Leaks.** Does the allow-list in §1 let any number forecast reach the package? Check:\n   - each allowed field's real content in stored stores, read-only (for example `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`):\n     `question`, evidence `one_line` and `quote`, source titles;\n   - whether evidence linked to a number question can itself be a system-written forecast rather than a source statement.\n\n   Name any path with a stored example.\n2. **Tables.** Are the state × event, value × reader and new path × old checks tables complete? Name any blank or wrong cell, for\n   example an event the export can meet that is not listed.\n3. **Tests and mutants.** Does each named test fail without the code it tests? Is a decisive case missing?\n4. **The $0 release check (§7).** Is the leak sweep sound? Consider the 12-character floor and the string classes. Would it miss a\n   forecast restated in different words?\n5. **The four open points in §8:**\n   - no idea submission in the release, with the idea acceptance moved to a later slice;\n   - `object` and `kind` on every record;\n   - groups left out;\n   - the sweep floor.\n\n   Decide each.\n6. **Ready to build?** Give a verdict: ready, or not ready with each serious finding.\n\n**Out of scope:** the judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen); the closed v13s line; the POC's own behaviour; any other open\ndefect; wording. Report only findings that change what is built or whether it is safe.\n**Not ready to build.** Both 74g overwrite findings are closed. Two issues remain in how the command reports success and how the tests verify it.\n\n1. **Both overwrite cases are closed.** `check` now creates the report with `os.link`. If a case-variant name already identifies the items database, the link fails and the database survives. `build` uses the same operation, so a file created at the report name while the build runs also survives. Tests 18 and 19 cover the database hash and the late-arriving marker respectively. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:56](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:56) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:363](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:363)\n\n2. **The builder can tell the operator a report is missing after it has published it.** Step 8 creates the public link, then removes the temporary name. If that removal fails, the complete report already exists, but the specified error says “report not written” and directs the operator to retry. A retry encounters the existing report and exits 2 again. Treat a successful link as the point when the report is published. A later cleanup error should identify the leftover temporary file. The decisive test forces only that removal to fail and verifies that the command correctly identifies the published report. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:192) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:200](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:200)\n\n3. **The end-to-end tests need an explicit expected exit status.** Test 11 says a successful build then “passes `check`,” but the build has already created the report, so the specified `check` command exits 2. Test 19 has the same issue while its marker occupies the report name. With the occupant in place, assert that `check` prints the successful package result, exits 2, and preserves the occupant. For the exit-0 case, remove the test-owned report first and verify that `check` creates a fresh one. This lets an engineer distinguish a valid package from a failed package check. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:204) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:342](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:342) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:366](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:366)\n\nI found no other serious blocker in slice 1.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
