{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,164p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: revision 9, for council round 74i. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\n     4\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\n     5\t\n     6\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\n     7\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\n     8\t- a missing source item is refused;\n     9\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\n    10\t- the manifest is a closed set;\n    11\t- the bound is validated as a date;\n    12\t- narrow reads;\n    13\t- size and speed budgets;\n    14\t- tests that separate every branch;\n    15\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\n    16\t- no idea submission.\n    17\t\n    18\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\n    19\t\n    20\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\n    21\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\n    22\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\n    23\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\n    24\t- The staging folder has one owner.\n    25\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\n    26\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\n    27\t\n    28\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\n    29\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\n    30\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\n    31\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\n    32\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\n    33\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\n    34\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\n    35\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\n    36\t\n    37\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\n    38\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\n    39\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\n    40\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\n    41\t\n    42\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\n    43\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\n    44\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\n    45\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\n    46\t  pause.\n    47\t\n    48\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r74f.md`.**\n    49\t- An explicit day is parsed first and used everywhere in its canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Python reads `20260825` as the same day,\n    50\t  but the stores compare days as text.\n    51\t- Neither command writes a report over an input database.\n    52\t\n    53\t**Revision 8 answers `codex-r74g.md` with one rule for every public write** (report writing drew findings in 74f and 74g). Nothing the\n    54\tbuild or `check` writes ever replaces an existing path:\n    55\t- the package is published by `publish` (`RENAME_EXCL`);\n    56\t- the report is published by writing a private temporary file, then `os.link` to the report name, which fails with `EEXIST` when\n    57\t  anything exists there.\n    58\t\n    59\tVerified on this Mac: `os.link` refuses an existing file, a case-variant name of it (`ITEMS.SQLITE` for `items.sqlite`), and a\n    60\tsymbolic link, leaving each untouched. An input database always exists, so no report can replace one. The path comparison of\n    61\trevision 7 is subsumed and dropped.\n    62\t\n    63\t**Revision 9 answers `codex-r74h.md`.**\n    64\t- A report is published the moment its link succeeds. A later failure to remove the temporary file is reported as published, naming\n    65\t  the leftover file.\n    66\t- `check`'s exit statuses are explicit, and the end-to-end tests assert them.\n    67\t\n    68\t## 0. Scope\n    69\t\n    70\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\n    71\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\n    72\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\n    73\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\n    74\t  - tests and mutants;\n    75\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\n    76\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\n    77\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\n    78\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\n    79\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\n    80\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\n    81\t- **Not in scope:**\n    82\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\n    83\t  - colleagues' page;\n    84\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\n    85\t  - any model call;\n    86\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\n    87\t\n    88\t## 1. What is built\n    89\t\n    90\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\n    91\t\n    92\t- **Constants:**\n    93\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\n    94\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\n    95\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\n    96\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\n    97\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\n    98\t\n    99\t  | Record | Keys |\n   100\t  |---|---|\n   101\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\n   102\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\n   103\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\n   104\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\n   105\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\n   106\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\n   107\t\n   108\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\n   109\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\n   110\t    only when the table exists;\n   111\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\n   112\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\n   113\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\n   114\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\n   115\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\n   116\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\n   117\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\n   118\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\n   119\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\n   120\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\n   121\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\n   122\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\n   123\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\n   124\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\n   125\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\n   126\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\n   127\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\n   128\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\n   129\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\n   130\t  - Value checks:\n   131\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\n   132\t    - `class` is in its set;\n   133\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\n   134\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\n   135\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\n   136\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\n   137\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\n   138\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\n   139\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\n   140\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\n   141\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\n   142\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\n   143\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\n   144\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\n   145\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\n   146\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\n   147\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\n   148\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\n   149\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\n   150\t\n   151\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\n   152\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\n   153\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\n   154\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\n   155\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\n   156\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\n   157\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\n   158\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\n   159\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\n   160\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\n   161\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\n   162\t\n   163\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\n   164\t  compared.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '165,330p'\"","aggregated_output":"   165\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\n   166\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\n   167\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\n   168\t  else.\n   169\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\n   170\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\n   171\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\n   172\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\n   173\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\n   174\t\n   175\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\n   176\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\n   177\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\n   178\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\n   179\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\n   180\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\n   181\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\n   182\t  - it returns the counts.\n   183\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\n   184\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\n   185\t\n   186\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\n   187\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\n   188\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\n   189\t     guarantee;\n   190\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\n   191\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\n   192\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\n   193\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\n   194\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\n   195\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\n   196\t     nothing;\n   197\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\n   198\t     `<out>.report.json`. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name. **A successful link is the moment the report\n   199\t     is published.** The temporary file is then removed. If that removal fails, the command still reports the report as published,\n   200\t     names the leftover temporary file, and exits 0.\n   201\t\n   202\t  The failure outcomes:\n   203\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\n   204\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\n   205\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\n   206\t  - **After publication, before the link** (step 8 fails before the link succeeds, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and\n   207\t    checked, and whatever is at the report name is untouched. Exit 2 with \"package published and checked; report not written; run\n   208\t    `check` to write it\".\n   209\t\n   210\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\n   211\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\n   212\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\n   213\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\n   214\t  - 0: the package passes, and the report was published;\n   215\t  - 2: the package passes, and the report name is occupied (an earlier report, or anything else), which stays untouched;\n   216\t  - 1: the package is refused, with the reason. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\n   217\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\n   218\t- **The report:**\n   219\t  - the store path and the bound;\n   220\t  - counts per class;\n   221\t  - the unresolved list;\n   222\t  - the fields compared;\n   223\t  - bytes;\n   224\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\n   225\t\n   226\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\n   227\t\n   228\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\n   229\t|---|---|---|---|\n   230\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\n   231\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \"no default day; supply --as-of\" | nothing | none |\n   232\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\n   233\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\n   234\t| The report name is occupied, by a file, a case-variant name of an input, or a symbolic link (build or `check`) | the build refuses at the start; a name occupied later makes `publish_report` fail with `EEXIST` and exit 2; `check` exits 2 after printing; whatever is there is untouched | the package only (build) | — |\n   235\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\n   236\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\n   237\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\n   238\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\n   239\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\n   240\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\n   241\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\n   242\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\n   243\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\n   244\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\n   245\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\n   246\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\n   247\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\n   248\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\n   249\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\n   250\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\n   251\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\n   252\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\n   253\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\n   254\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\n   255\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\n   256\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\n   257\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\n   258\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\n   259\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\n   260\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n   261\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\n   262\t\n   263\t## 3. Value × reader\n   264\t\n   265\tReaders of the package:\n   266\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\n   267\t- the release page (slice 2);\n   268\t- the tests.\n   269\t\n   270\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\n   271\t\n   272\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\n   273\t|---|---|---|\n   274\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\n   275\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\n   276\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\n   277\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\n   278\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\n   279\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\n   280\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\n   281\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\n   282\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\n   283\t\n   284\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\n   285\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\n   286\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\n   287\t- `view_switches.reason`;\n   288\t- `clean_ladders`;\n   289\t- `thesis_groups`;\n   290\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\n   291\t\n   292\t## 4. New path × old checks\n   293\t\n   294\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\n   295\t|---|---|\n   296\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\n   297\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\n   298\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\n   299\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\n   300\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\n   301\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\n   302\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\n   303\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\n   304\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\n   305\t\n   306\t## 5. Prior decisions\n   307\t\n   308\t- D726: number questions show sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\n   309\t- D756: Alex's choice.\n   310\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\n   311\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\n   312\t- D12/D13: no clock.\n   313\t- D163: English product text.\n   314\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\n   315\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\n   316\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\n   317\t\n   318\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\n   319\t\n   320\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\n   321\tits row above:\n   322\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\n   323\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\n   324\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\n   325\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\n   326\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\n   327\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\n   328\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\n   329\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\n   330\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '331,500p'; cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\"","aggregated_output":"   331\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\n   332\t   \"$1 trillion\" is absent.\n   333\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\": `event`, with its label kept. A\n   334\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\n   335\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\n   336\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\n   337\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\n   338\t9. **Package:**\n   339\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\n   340\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\n   341\t   - a changed data byte fails;\n   342\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\n   343\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\n   344\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\n   345\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\n   346\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\n   347\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\n   348\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\n   349\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\n   350\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\n   351\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted):\n   352\t    - the build exits 0, and the package and its report exist;\n   353\t    - `check` with the build's report still in place prints a passing result and exits 2;\n   354\t    - after the test removes that report, `check` exits 0 and publishes a fresh one.\n   355\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\n   356\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\n   357\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\" is introduced.\n   358\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\n   359\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\n   360\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\n   361\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\n   362\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\n   363\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\n   364\t14. **The publication rule.**\n   365\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\n   366\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\n   367\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\n   368\t      afterwards, empty.\n   369\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\n   370\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\n   371\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\n   372\t      and inode).\n   373\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\n   374\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\n   375\t18. **Report over an input.** `--out` is chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database, three ways: the same path, a\n   376\t    case-variant name on this case-insensitive volume, and a symbolic link to it. `build` refuses, and `check` on an existing package\n   377\t    exits 2. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\n   378\t19. **Report name taken during the build** (a scratch copy with a pause just before `publish_report`): the test writes a marker file\n   379\t    at the report name. The command exits 2 and the marker is unchanged. `check` then prints a passing result, exits 2, and leaves the\n   380\t    marker unchanged.\n   381\t20. **Temporary file left after the link** (a scratch copy in which removing the report's temporary file raises): the build exits 0\n   382\t    and says the report is published, naming the leftover temporary file. The report exists and equals the build's report.\n   383\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\n   384\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\n   385\t15. **Files:**\n   386\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\n   387\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\n   388\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\n   389\t16. **Bound validation:**\n   390\t    - `2026-08-99` is refused;\n   391\t    - `20260825` is refused, while `2026-08-25` builds. On a fixture with evidence on both sides of that day, the package holds only\n   392\t      the earlier evidence;\n   393\t    - a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\n   394\t\n   395\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\n   396\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\n   397\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\n   398\t- the event test removed;\n   399\t- the Yes/No test removed;\n   400\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\n   401\t- manifest keys unchecked;\n   402\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\n   403\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\n   404\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\n   405\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\n   406\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\n   407\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\n   408\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\n   409\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\n   410\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\n   411\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\n   412\t- the canonical-day check removed (test 16's `20260825` then builds with later evidence);\n   413\t- `publish_report` replaced by `os.replace` (tests 18 and 19 then overwrite the items file and the marker);\n   414\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\n   415\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\n   416\t- the switch reason emitted;\n   417\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\n   418\t\n   419\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\n   420\t\n   421\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\n   422\tserved ledger with its items database.\n   423\t\n   424\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\n   425\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\n   426\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\n   427\t\n   428\tThe steps:\n   429\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\n   430\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\n   431\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\n   432\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\n   433\t   - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\n   434\t   - the genuine analyst \"$390 billion\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\n   435\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\"About $390 billion…\") substituted into\n   436\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\n   437\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\n   438\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\n   439\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\n   440\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \"around $1 trillion\" text and j865's band text are absent.\n   441\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\n   442\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\"due …, frozen on … at\n   443\t   rung N <label>\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\n   444\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\n   445\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\n   446\t   - rung labels and conditions;\n   447\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\n   448\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\n   449\t   - switch reasons.\n   450\t\n   451\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\n   452\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \"Bullish\", is recorded as such.\n   453\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\n   454\t\n   455\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\n   456\t\n   457\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\n   458\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \"more than $40 billion in\n   459\tFY2028\" for a quote's \"more than double that next year\".\n   460\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\n   461\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\n   462\t  sentence. One restates \"close to doubling\" as \"nearly 100%\".\n   463\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\n   464\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \"takes\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\n   465\t  judged position.\n   466\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\n   467\t  reproduces.\n   468\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\n   469\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \"amounts as quoted\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\n   470\t    as `e3238`'s \"more than $40 billion\".\n   471\t  - Claude reads it as \"the release computes or converts nothing\".\n   472\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\n   473\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\n   474\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\n   475\t  allow-list or change it.\n# \"Forecast unavailable\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\n\n**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\n- D726, \"同意\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\",\n  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \"it is built with the release work, which is not started\";\n- D756, \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\".\n\nOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\n\n**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\ncould reach a reader:\n- the idea card;\n- the closing text;\n- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\n- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\n- a translated export;\n- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\n\nA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\nstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\n\n## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\n\nThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\n- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\n- **Its idea input** reads \"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\".\n- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\n  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \"around $1 trillion\" for 2027 spending;\n  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\n\n  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\n\n## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\n\n- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\n  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\n- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\n  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\n  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\n- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\n  - no live POC service;\n  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\n  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\n  - no `--composite-trials` input.\n\n  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\n- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\n  - the question and its id;\n  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\n  - the marker \"Forecast unavailable\".\n\n  Nothing else is listed:\n  - no ladder;\n  - no band, label or condition;\n  - no reasons or why_changed;\n  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\n  - no closing band (\"closed\" only);\n  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\n- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\n  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\n  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\n  delivered card.\n- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\n  later choice for Alex.\n\n## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\n\nA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\n1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\n   questions in the three comparison stores.\n2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\n   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\n   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\n\nEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\n(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\n(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\n\nCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\n- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\n- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\n\nNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\n\n**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\nbinary event such as \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\nevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\n\n## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n\nD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\nallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\n- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\n  readers would see.\n- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\n  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\n- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\n  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\n  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\n  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\n- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\n  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\n  `why_changed`.\n- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\n  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\n\n## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\n\n- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\n  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\n  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\n  - an unresolved one with a key;\n  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\n  - an event question;\n  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\n  - a real closing switch;\n  - an idea.\n- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\n  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\n  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\n- **Mutants:**\n  - an extra field;\n  - a fetch left on;\n  - a ladder read in idea composition;\n  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\n\n  Each must fail.\n- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\n  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with no scored driver and no\n    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\n  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\n    prose rule.\n- **The $0 release check.**\n  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\n    final band there.\n  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\n  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\n  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\n\n## 6. Not in scope\n\n- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\n- The closed v13s line.\n- Other open defects.\n- No prompt or pipeline change.\n- The POC's own behaviour.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{RELEASE-BUILD,FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN}.md; head -65 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n '\"'^#{1,3} .*D(726|756|757|758)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{RELEASE-BUILD,FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN}.md; head -65 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; rg -n '\"'^#{1,3} .*D(726|756|757|758)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"     201 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\n    1232 docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\n     475 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md\n     147 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\n    2055 total\n# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \"Forecast unavailable\" into the first release\n11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '151,351p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '151,351p'\"","aggregated_output":"   151\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\n   152\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\n   153\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\n   154\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\n   155\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\n   156\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\n   157\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\n   158\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\n   159\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\n   160\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\n   161\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\n   162\t\n   163\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\n   164\t  compared.\n   165\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\n   166\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\n   167\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\n   168\t  else.\n   169\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\n   170\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\n   171\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\n   172\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\n   173\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\n   174\t\n   175\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\n   176\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\n   177\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\n   178\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\n   179\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\n   180\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\n   181\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\n   182\t  - it returns the counts.\n   183\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\n   184\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\n   185\t\n   186\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\n   187\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\n   188\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` or `<out>.report.json` early, as a convenience. The no-replace publication of each holds the\n   189\t     guarantee;\n   190\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\n   191\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\n   192\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\n   193\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\n   194\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\n   195\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\n   196\t     nothing;\n   197\t  8. `publish_report`: write the report to a private temporary file in the same folder (`tempfile.mkstemp`), then `os.link` it to\n   198\t     `<out>.report.json`. The link fails with `EEXIST` if anything exists at that name. **A successful link is the moment the report\n   199\t     is published.** The temporary file is then removed. If that removal fails, the command still reports the report as published,\n   200\t     names the leftover temporary file, and exits 0.\n   201\t\n   202\t  The failure outcomes:\n   203\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\n   204\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\n   205\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\n   206\t  - **After publication, before the link** (step 8 fails before the link succeeds, including `EEXIST`): the package is final and\n   207\t    checked, and whatever is at the report name is untouched. Exit 2 with \"package published and checked; report not written; run\n   208\t    `check` to write it\".\n   209\t\n   210\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\n   211\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical\n   212\t  `as_of` validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place, prints\n   213\t  the report, and writes `<out>.report.json` only through `publish_report`, so it never replaces anything. Its exit statuses:\n   214\t  - 0: the package passes, and the report was published;\n   215\t  - 2: the package passes, and the report name is occupied (an earlier report, or anything else), which stays untouched;\n   216\t  - 1: the package is refused, with the reason. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\n   217\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\n   218\t- **The report:**\n   219\t  - the store path and the bound;\n   220\t  - counts per class;\n   221\t  - the unresolved list;\n   222\t  - the fields compared;\n   223\t  - bytes;\n   224\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\n   225\t\n   226\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\n   227\t\n   228\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\n   229\t|---|---|---|---|\n   230\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\n   231\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \"no default day; supply --as-of\" | nothing | none |\n   232\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\n   233\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\n   234\t| The report name is occupied, by a file, a case-variant name of an input, or a symbolic link (build or `check`) | the build refuses at the start; a name occupied later makes `publish_report` fail with `EEXIST` and exit 2; `check` exits 2 after printing; whatever is there is untouched | the package only (build) | — |\n   235\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\n   236\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\n   237\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\n   238\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\n   239\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\n   240\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\n   241\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\n   242\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\n   243\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\n   244\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\n   245\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\n   246\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\n   247\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\n   248\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\n   249\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\n   250\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\n   251\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\n   252\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\n   253\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\n   254\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\n   255\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\n   256\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\n   257\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\n   258\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\n   259\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\n   260\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n   261\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\n   262\t\n   263\t## 3. Value × reader\n   264\t\n   265\tReaders of the package:\n   266\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\n   267\t- the release page (slice 2);\n   268\t- the tests.\n   269\t\n   270\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\n   271\t\n   272\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\n   273\t|---|---|---|\n   274\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\n   275\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\n   276\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\n   277\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\n   278\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\n   279\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\n   280\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\n   281\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\n   282\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\n   283\t\n   284\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\n   285\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\n   286\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\n   287\t- `view_switches.reason`;\n   288\t- `clean_ladders`;\n   289\t- `thesis_groups`;\n   290\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\n   291\t\n   292\t## 4. New path × old checks\n   293\t\n   294\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\n   295\t|---|---|\n   296\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\n   297\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\n   298\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\n   299\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\n   300\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\n   301\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\n   302\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\n   303\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\n   304\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\n   305\t\n   306\t## 5. Prior decisions\n   307\t\n   308\t- D726: number questions show sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\n   309\t- D756: Alex's choice.\n   310\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\n   311\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\n   312\t- D12/D13: no clock.\n   313\t- D163: English product text.\n   314\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\n   315\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\n   316\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\n   317\t\n   318\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\n   319\t\n   320\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\n   321\tits row above:\n   322\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\n   323\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\n   324\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\n   325\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\n   326\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\n   327\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\n   328\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\n   329\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\n   330\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\n   331\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\n   332\t   \"$1 trillion\" is absent.\n   333\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\": `event`, with its label kept. A\n   334\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\n   335\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\n   336\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\n   337\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\n   338\t9. **Package:**\n   339\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\n   340\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\n   341\t   - a changed data byte fails;\n   342\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\n   343\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\n   344\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\n   345\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\n   346\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\n   347\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\n   348\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\n   349\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\n   350\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\n   351\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
