{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10991,11009p;11823,11905p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; tail -4 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md; tail -n +66 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\"","aggregated_output":"## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n\n- **The questions** (after D725):\n  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n    (recommended); 暂不定.\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n    ceiling.\n  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n- poc-v118 stays the product.\n\n## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\n\n## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n\n- **The question** (after D755): \"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\"\n  - Options:\n    - \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\": the council's consensus;\n    - \"换更强的模型再小测一次\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\n    - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\n  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n    forecast text and the history withheld together.\n  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\" appear.\n- **Kept for the record, not built:**\n  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\n  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\n  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\n\n## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n\n- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \"Forecast\n  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\n- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\n  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\n  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\n- **The design, after four review rounds** (`codex-r72.md` … `codex-r72d.md`):\n  - one release exporter with an explicit allow-list, called directly by the release builder; the finished package is checked;\n  - for a number question, the allow-list holds only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\";\n  - the release reads nothing else: no live POC service, no translated or prepared JSON, no composite trials;\n  - identity is structural: a question is a number question unless it is an event measure or a canonical Yes/No pair, and unresolved\n    records are withheld and listed. Verified on four stores with no wrong result;\n  - tests, mutants and an end-to-end acceptance on `old-1/v8` and the two known event leaks.\n  - **Why an allow-list.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new leak paths in a reader-by-reader design, so revision 3 replaced that\n    approach with one structural rule.\n- **Open for Alex:**\n  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\n  2. what questions that are not number questions show in the release:\n     - (a) answer and label without explanation text, recommended by the council and Claude;\n     - (b) explanations only where the judge was shown no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions at the latest answer, and it\n       cannot guarantee that no number forecast is quoted.\n- **Not done.** Nothing is built and nothing is committed. The POC is unchanged.\n\n## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n\n- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\n  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\n  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\n- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\n  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\n     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\n     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \"not started\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\n  2. **§4 (a):** an event or Yes/No question shows its question, evidence and answer with its original label, and no generated\n     explanation. It alone guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose (option (b) cannot: a request carries the\n     question's earlier reasoning, `views/judging.py:211`). The cost is real: readers lose the written rationale for those answers.\n  3. **The v13s checker defects** (`PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5) are closed as won't-fix: `calc_small.py` has callers only in research\n     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\n  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\n     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\n- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\"自己的量，别的期间\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n  system (D263).\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n  competition or pricing\".\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n  of the previous filing topic).\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n\n## 5. What to do\n\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n     the existing rule).\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n  measured and reported apart.\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n  counted after.\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n    question\";\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^def (resolve_bound|view_exists|is_open_as_of|state_as_of|evidence|evidence_record|ladder_bands)|original_who|original_day'\"' src/hivemind/service.py; rg -n '\"'^def (read_snapshot|item_lookup|view_bundle|library)|evidence'\"' src/hivemind/bundle.py; rg -n 'create table (views|rungs|evidence)|def (view_key|rungs_of|create_view|insert)' -i src/hivemind/views/store.py; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod; rg -n 'served ledger|views.sqlite|items.*sqlite' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^def (resolve_bound|view_exists|is_open_as_of|state_as_of|evidence|evidence_record|ladder_bands)|original_who|original_day'\"' src/hivemind/service.py; rg -n '\"'^def (read_snapshot|item_lookup|view_bundle|library)|evidence'\"' src/hivemind/bundle.py; rg -n 'create table (views|rungs|evidence)|def (view_key|rungs_of|create_view|insert)' -i src/hivemind/views/store.py; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod; rg -n 'served ledger|views.sqlite|items.*sqlite' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md\"","aggregated_output":"57:def resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\n118:def view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n122:def is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\n129:def state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\n224:def evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\n233:            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\n238:def evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\n499:def ladder_bands(rungs):\n2:evidence it cited, the evidence in force with tiers, speakers and sources, dependencies, replacements and the freeze\n14:def read_snapshot(*connections):\n28:def item_lookup(items_db):\n100:def view_bundle(views_db, item_of, view_id, as_of=None):\n121:                           'why_changed': j['why_changed'], 'reasons': j['reasons'], 'cited': list(dict.fromkeys(json.loads(j['cited_evidence_json'] or '[]'))),   # each id once (UI contract uniqueItems); the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger holds one judgement citing an id twice\n124:    evidence = []\n125:    for e in views_db.execute('select e.*, l.seq as linked_seq from evidence_links l join evidence e on e.evidence_id=l.evidence_id where l.view_id=? order by l.id', (view_id,)):\n128:        sources = [dict(s) for s in views_db.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (e['evidence_id'],))\n130:        replaced_by = views_db.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n133:        replaces = views_db.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (e['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n138:        evidence.append({'id': e['evidence_id'], 'one_line': e['one_line'], 'quote': e['quote'], 'tier': e['tier'], 'speaker': e['speaker'],\n147:                         'outlets': len(sources), 'replaced_by': {'new_evidence_id': replaced_by['new_evidence_id'], 'said_day': replaced_by['said_day'],\n149:                         'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces else None})\n172:            'judgements': judgements, 'evidence': evidence, 'dependencies': dependencies, 'dependants': dependants,\n225:def library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n75:def insert(conn, table, **fields):\n83:def create_view(conn, *, view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, rungs, seq, input_id, created_at):\n97:def rungs_of(conn, view_id):\n159:def view_key(conn, view_id):\narchive.sqlite\nmanifests\nreplay.log\nviews.sqlite\n23:     served ledger's \"Restriction adopted\" labels, and a legacy store with no key table;\n43:  and 25.4% of the evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and on 35.0% in the served ledger\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '49,153p;204,268p;480,527p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '10,45p;220,256p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/service.py | sed -n '49,153p;204,268p;480,527p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/bundle.py | sed -n '10,45p;220,256p'\"","aggregated_output":"    49\t        self.start, self.end = start, end\n    50\t        super().__init__(f'range start after its end: {start} to {end}')\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tdef first_day_unfinished(conn):\n    54\t    return store.last_completed_day(conn) is None and conn.execute('select 1 from processing_steps limit 1').fetchone() is not None\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef resolve_bound(conn, bound, *, unfiltered=False):\n    58\t    \"\"\"The one owner of an upper date bound, explicit or omitted (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3).\n    59\t\n    60\t    A store whose first day is in progress is refused. An omitted bound is today's default day; with `unfiltered` (the bundle\n    61\t    functions, whose omitted bound read every record), it is the last completed day, or None (no filter, as before) on a store with\n    62\t    none. An explicit bound later than the last completed day is refused, whatever the store holds after it; one on or before it\n    63\t    passes. Idempotent: a bound it passed passes again.\"\"\"\n    64\t    if first_day_unfinished(conn):\n    65\t        raise FirstDayNotCompleted()\n    66\t    last = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    67\t    if not bound:\n    68\t        return last if unfiltered else default_as_of(conn)\n    69\t    if last is not None and bound > last:\n    70\t        raise BoundNotCompleted(bound, last)\n    71\t    return bound\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\tdef resolve_range(conn, start, end):\n    75\t    \"\"\"A range's end resolved by `resolve_bound` (an explicit future end is refused there); a start after the end is refused. A start\n    76\t    equal to the end reads as before: an empty window for `changes`, whose start is excluded, and that one day for `history`, whose\n    77\t    start is included; a client polling \"what changed since the day I last saw\" keeps its empty answer until a day completes\n    78\t    (council round 124). An end that resolves to None (an empty store) is compared with nothing, as before.\"\"\"\n    79\t    end = resolve_bound(conn, end)\n    80\t    if start and end is not None and start > end:\n    81\t        raise RangeNotOrdered(start, end)\n    82\t    return end\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t_SEQ_DAYS = {}      # id(connection) → (connection, (max sequence, rows), map); a sqlite3 connection cannot carry attributes\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\tdef seq_day_map(conn):\n    89\t    \"\"\"sequence number → the publication day of the item or daily round written under it. Cached per connection and\n    90\t    rebuilt when processing_steps has grown (an open ledger gains steps while the pipeline runs); without the cache\n    91\t    one view with 367 pieces of evidence cost 1,224 full scans (0.46 s, measured 2026-10-24).\"\"\"\n    92\t    stamp = tuple(conn.execute('select max(sequence_no), count(*) from processing_steps').fetchone())\n    93\t    entry = _SEQ_DAYS.get(id(conn))\n    94\t    if entry is not None and entry[0] is conn and entry[1] == stamp:\n    95\t        return entry[2]\n    96\t    cache = {}\n    97\t    for seq, day in conn.execute('select sequence_no, min(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0 group by sequence_no'):\n    98\t        cache[seq] = day\n    99\t    if cache:                 # sequence 0 is the seed questions written before the first item (D253): visible from the ledger's first day\n   100\t        cache[0] = min(cache.values())\n   101\t    if len(_SEQ_DAYS) >= 64:\n   102\t        _SEQ_DAYS.clear()\n   103\t    _SEQ_DAYS[id(conn)] = (conn, stamp, cache)\n   104\t    return cache\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\tdef day_of_seq(conn, seq):\n   108\t    return seq_day_map(conn).get(seq)\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef visible(conn, seq, as_of):\n   112\t    day = day_of_seq(conn, seq)\n   113\t    return day is not None and day <= as_of\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\t# ---------- views\n   117\t\n   118\tdef view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n   119\t    return visible(conn, record['created_seq'], as_of)\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\tdef is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\n   123\t    for row in conn.execute('select open, after_seq from view_switches where view_id=? order by id desc', (view_id,)):\n   124\t        if visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\n   125\t            return bool(row['open'])\n   126\t    return True\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of):\n   130\t    \"\"\"The last judgement on or before the day, with the day the current position was first taken.\"\"\"\n   131\t    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id', (view_id, as_of))]\n   132\t    if not rows:\n   133\t        return None\n   134\t    last = rows[-1]\n   135\t    since, previous = last['publication_day'], None\n   136\t    for row in reversed(rows[:-1]):\n   137\t        if row['rung'] != last['rung']:\n   138\t            previous = row['rung']\n   139\t            break\n   140\t        since = row['publication_day']\n   141\t    return {'position': last['rung'], 'judgement_day': last['publication_day'], 'since_day': since, 'previous_position': previous,\n   142\t            'rounds': len(rows), 'why_changed': last['why_changed'], 'reasons': last['reasons'], 'theme_pushes': _json(last.get('theme_pushes_json'))}\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\tdef summaries(conn, as_of=None, include_closed=False):\n   146\t    \"\"\"Every view as of the day as a light record (id, object, kind, what it looks at, the question, due day, open,\n   147\t    dependency and dependant ids): what a search ranks. The full record with its evidence counts is `view`; listing\n   148\t    92 of those cost 0.29 s per search (1,205 evidence reads), measured 2026-10-24.\"\"\"\n   149\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\n   150\t    out = []\n   151\t    for record in conn.execute('select * from views order by created_seq'):\n   152\t        record = dict(record)\n   153\t        if not view_exists(conn, record, as_of):\n   204\t        return None\n   205\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   206\t    state = state_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of)\n   207\t    if state:\n   208\t        rung = next((r for r in rungs if r['position'] == state['position']), None)\n   209\t        state['label'] = rung['label'] if rung else None\n   210\t        state['condition'] = rung['condition'] if rung else None\n   211\t    in_force = evidence(conn, view_id, as_of)\n   212\t    return {\n   213\t        'view_id': view_id, 'object': record['object_id'], 'object_kind': record['object_kind'], 'kind': record['kind'],\n   214\t        'looks_at': record['looks_at'], 'question': record['question'], 'due_day': record['due_day'], 'year': record['year'],\n   215\t        'created_day': day_of_seq(conn, record['created_seq']), 'created_from': record['created_from_input'],\n   216\t        'as_of': as_of, 'open': is_open_as_of(conn, view_id, as_of), 'rungs': rungs, 'state': state,\n   217\t        'dependencies': dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of), 'dependants': dependants(conn, view_id, as_of),\n   218\t        'counts': {'rounds': state['rounds'] if state else 0, 'evidence': len(in_force), 'facts': sum(1 for e in in_force if vocabulary.canonical('tier', e['tier']) == TIER_FACT)},\n   219\t    }\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t# ---------- evidence\n   223\t\n   224\tdef evidence_record(conn, evidence_id, as_of, arrived_seq=None):\n   225\t    \"\"\"One piece of evidence with only the sources recorded on or before the day (a later outlet of the same\n   226\t    sentence is not yet known on that day).\"\"\"\n   227\t    piece = store.evidence(conn, evidence_id)\n   228\t    if not piece:\n   229\t        return None\n   230\t    sources = [dict(s) for s in conn.execute('select input_id, category, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,)) if visible(conn, s['seq'], as_of)]\n   231\t    replaces = conn.execute('select old_evidence_id, seq from replacements where new_evidence_id=?', (evidence_id,)).fetchone()\n   232\t    return {'evidence_id': piece['evidence_id'], 'one_line': piece['one_line'], 'quote': piece['quote'], 'tier': piece['tier'],\n   233\t            'speaker': piece['speaker'], 'original_who': piece['original_who'], 'original_day': piece['original_day'], 'event_time': piece['event_time'],\n   234\t            'day': day_of_seq(conn, arrived_seq if arrived_seq is not None else piece['created_seq']), 'sources': sources, 'outlets': len(sources),\n   235\t            'replaces': replaces['old_evidence_id'] if replaces and visible(conn, replaces['seq'], as_of) else None}\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\tdef evidence(conn, view_id, as_of=None, tier=None):\n   239\t    \"\"\"Evidence linked to the view on or before the day and not replaced on or before it, with its sources.\"\"\"\n   240\t    as_of = resolve_bound(conn, as_of)\n   241\t    out = []\n   242\t    for link in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)):\n   243\t        if not visible(conn, link['seq'], as_of):\n   244\t            continue\n   245\t        replacement = conn.execute('select new_evidence_id, said_day, seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n   246\t        if replacement and visible(conn, replacement['seq'], as_of):\n   247\t            continue\n   248\t        piece = evidence_record(conn, link['evidence_id'], as_of, link['seq'])\n   249\t        if tier and piece['tier'] != tier:\n   250\t            continue\n   251\t        out.append(piece)\n   252\t    return out\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\t# ---------- history\n   256\t\n   257\tdef history(conn, view_id, from_day=None, to_day=None):\n   258\t    to_day = resolve_range(conn, from_day, to_day)\n   259\t    from_day = from_day or '0000-00-00'\n   260\t    judgements = []\n   261\t    previous = None\n   262\t    for row in conn.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id', (view_id,)):\n   263\t        entry = {'day': row['publication_day'], 'seq': row['seq'], 'position': row['rung'], 'changed': bool(row['changed']), 'moved_from': previous if previous is not None and previous != row['rung'] else None,\n   264\t                 'why_changed': row['why_changed'], 'reasons': row['reasons'], 'cited': _unique(_json(row['cited_evidence_json'])), 'pushes': _json(row['pushes_json']),\n   265\t                 'theme_pushes': _json(row['theme_pushes_json'] if 'theme_pushes_json' in row.keys() else None), 'round': row['input_id']}\n   266\t        previous = row['rung']\n   267\t        if from_day <= row['publication_day'] <= to_day:\n   268\t            judgements.append(entry)\n   480\t    if not found:\n   481\t        return None\n   482\t    if lo > hi or (lo == hi and not (lo_inc and hi_inc)):\n   483\t        return None\n   484\t    return (lo, lo_inc, hi, hi_inc)\n   485\t\n   486\t\n   487\tdef numeric_bands(rungs):\n   488\t    \"\"\"Bands from the rungs' own numeric bounds (keyed views): lower bound inclusive, upper exclusive, the two ends open;\n   489\t    None when a rung has no bounds.\"\"\"\n   490\t    if not rungs or any(r.get('lo') is None and r.get('hi') is None for r in rungs):\n   491\t        return None\n   492\t    out = {}\n   493\t    for r in rungs:\n   494\t        lo = -INF if r.get('lo') is None else float(r['lo']); hi = INF if r.get('hi') is None else float(r['hi'])\n   495\t        out[r['position']] = (lo, True, hi, False)\n   496\t    return out\n   497\t\n   498\t\n   499\tdef ladder_bands(rungs):\n   500\t    \"\"\"Every rung's band, or None with the reason when the ladder is not one unbroken partition by amount. Rungs that\n   501\t    carry numeric bounds are read from them; the prose parser serves the views written before keys.\"\"\"\n   502\t    numeric = numeric_bands(rungs)\n   503\t    if numeric is not None:\n   504\t        ordered = sorted(numeric.items(), key=lambda pb: pb[1][0])\n   505\t        for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\n   506\t            if a[2] != b[0]:\n   507\t                return None, f'numeric bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\n   508\t        return numeric, None\n   509\t    bands = [(r['position'], band(r['condition'])) for r in rungs]\n   510\t    unreadable = [p for p, b in bands if b is None]\n   511\t    if unreadable:\n   512\t        return None, f'conditions not read as amounts: positions {unreadable}'\n   513\t    ordered = sorted(bands, key=lambda pb: (pb[1][0], pb[1][2]))\n   514\t    for (p1, a), (p2, b) in zip(ordered, ordered[1:]):\n   515\t        if a[2] != b[0] or a[3] == b[1]:          # adjacent bands share the boundary amount and exactly one of them owns it\n   516\t            return None, f'bands of positions {p1} and {p2} overlap or leave a gap'\n   517\t    lowest, highest = ordered[0][1], ordered[-1][1]\n   518\t    if not (lowest[0] == -INF or (lowest[0] == 0 and lowest[1])) or highest[2] != INF:     # an amount that cannot be negative may start at 0\n   519\t        return None, 'the ladder does not cover the line up to +inf'\n   520\t    return dict(bands), None\n   521\t\n   522\t\n   523\tdef _contains(b, yi):\n   524\t    lo, lo_inc, hi, hi_inc = b\n   525\t    return (lo < yi or (lo == yi and lo_inc)) and (yi < hi or (yi == hi and hi_inc))\n   526\t\n   527\t\n    10\tfrom .views import store\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\t@contextmanager\n    14\tdef read_snapshot(*connections):\n    15\t    \"\"\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\"\"\"\n    16\t    owned = []\n    17\t    try:\n    18\t        for conn in connections:\n    19\t            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\n    20\t                conn.execute('begin')\n    21\t                owned.append(conn)\n    22\t        yield\n    23\t    finally:\n    24\t        for conn in reversed(owned):\n    25\t            conn.rollback()\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef item_lookup(items_db):\n    29\t    \"\"\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\n    30\t    database is not given or does not hold it).\"\"\"\n    31\t    cache = {}\n    32\t\n    33\t    def item_of(input_id):\n    34\t        if input_id not in cache:\n    35\t            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None\n    36\t            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}\n    37\t        return cache[input_id]\n    38\t    return item_of\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef _visible(views_db, seq, as_of):\n    42\t    return as_of is None or service.visible(views_db, seq, as_of)\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\tdef ladder_row(views_db, view_id):\n   220\t    \"\"\"Selected complete thesis records, pinned to one read transaction.\"\"\"\n   221\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\n   222\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\tdef library(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n   226\t    \"\"\"All theses, including closed ones, and stored groups; no search or model call.\"\"\"\n   227\t    with read_snapshot(views_db, items_db):\n   228\t        as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\n   229\t        if not as_of:\n   230\t            raise ValueError('The library has no completed day; supply as_of')\n   231\t        date.fromisoformat(as_of)\n   232\t        view_ids = [r['view_id'] for r in views_db.execute('select * from views order by created_seq, rowid')\n   233\t                    if service.view_exists(views_db, r, as_of)]\n   234\t        if not view_ids:\n   235\t            return {'as_of': as_of, 'days': days(views_db, as_of), 'views': [], 'coverage': 'library', 'groups': []}\n   236\t        return _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
