{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'sealed|poc/data/.+sqlite|served' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{codex-r74,claude-r74b,claude-r74c,codex-r72}.md; rg --files --hidden --no-ignore poc | rg 'items-comparison.sqlite\"'$|views.sqlite$'\"' | head -80\"","aggregated_output":"rg: docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74b.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74c.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72.md:10:   **The proposed number-question rule fits the three comparison stores but fails on supported data.** I counted numeric bounds on 19/47, 17/43 and 18/49 questions in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`. On the sealed ledger used by the service tests, Data Center revenue `v3` has no `lo` or `hi` columns at all. Yet `evaluate(v3, >= $300B)` returned `holds` and the judged $300–350B range. The reverse case also exists. Stored Xbox question `v37` has explicit **Yes/No** answers with numeric bounds around zero. The current opening check accepts a ladder with every bound null. Define identity by the kind of answer the question asks for, cover both stored examples, and specify what the release does when an older record is ambiguous. The existing helper for linking questions has a narrower, asset-only purpose. [tests/test_service.py:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:18) · [tests/test_service.py:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:119) · [stored Xbox ledger:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:20) · [extraction.py:493](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [links.py:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:144)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:5:I checked the three comparison stores and the served ledger read-only. I found **no confirmed case of a stored judgement being copied into an evidence record**. I did find a meaningful difference between the article, the system’s summary of it, and the system’s own answer. The build design treats all three as strings.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md:33:- **Tests 3, 4, 5, 6 and 11** need fixtures that distinguish the branches. Defaulting to `number` passes test 3 even if the unresolved report lists every number question. Assert a condition-only *resolved* question is absent from that report and an unresolved one is present, both with and without a key. For test 6 use the served ledger’s `v49` labels, **“Restriction adopted” / “No restriction adopted.”** All 85 comparison-store events also have Yes/No labels, so removing event recognition can leave the displayed answer unchanged. Exercise the legacy case with the key table genuinely absent. [Tests:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:168) · [Event overlap:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:85) · [Legacy lookup:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:159)\npoc/reports/2026-10-25-full-day-parallel-r4/serial/views.sqlite\npoc/reports/2026-10-25-full-day-parallel-r4/parallel/views.sqlite\npoc/data/old-2026-10-23-run3a/views.sqlite\npoc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite\npoc/data/english-groups-2026-10-25/views.sqlite\npoc/data/english-v33-nvda-week-2026-10-27/views.sqlite\npoc/data/clean-stage-b-2026-11-11/draw-u1/views.sqlite\npoc/data/e2e-v69-seed2-d3/views.sqlite\npoc/data/e2e-v69-dev14-d2/views.sqlite\npoc/data/clean-stage-b-2026-11-11/draw-u3/views.sqlite\npoc/data/clean-stage-b-2026-11-11/draw-u2/views.sqlite\npoc/data/english-v29-theme-r5-2026-10-26/views.sqlite\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/new-2/judge/draw-new-2/views.sqlite\npoc/data/review-v118-old2-0920-2026-1