{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/README.md; sed -n '1,110p' src/hivemind/views/store.py; cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74{e,f,g}.md | head -46\"","aggregated_output":"# Served copy of the sealed 2026-10-28 ledger, minus v68\n\n`views.sqlite` = `sealed-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` with thesis v68 removed (Alex, 2026-10-28 17:05:\n\"你直接把它移除，这是我们自己的失误\"). v68, \"What stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for calendar 2027?\", was opened on the\nrun's last day by the succession rule (same quantity, next period, after v24) and the writer linked its one opening statement to\nv7 and v24 instead of to it, so it stood with no evidence and no judgement. Rows removed: views, view_keys, rungs, successions,\nview_switches, views_fts for v68 (no evidence_links or judgements existed). The sealed folder is untouched and remains the record;\nthe front end, the API and the page build read this copy.\n\"\"\"The views database (docs/prd/06-views.md): append-only tables for views, rungs, judgements, evidence, links,\nreplacements, dependencies, successions, match records, processing steps and the review pool; a trigram\nfull-text index over the views for the matching lists; the queries the other modules read.\n\nEvery table refuses UPDATE and DELETE (triggers). Progress and counts are rows, never updates. There is no item\ntext here: evidence holds the quoted sentence and the one-line restatement only.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sqlite3\n\nTABLES = {\n    'views': 'view_id text primary key, object_id text, object_kind text, kind text, looks_at text, question text, due_day text, year text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text, created_at text',\n    'rungs': 'view_id text, position integer, label text, condition text, lo real, hi real',\n    'view_keys': 'view_id text primary key, measure text, scope text, scope_key text, period_start text, period_end text, basis text, unit text, event_type text, seq integer, scope_source text, key_version integer',\n    'view_switches': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, open integer, reason text, by_whom text, after_seq integer',\n    'judgements': 'judgement_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, rung integer, reasons text, cited_evidence_json text, cited_views_json text, pushes_json text, changed integer, why_changed text, config_checksum text, call_id integer, request_sha256 text, publication_day text, theme_pushes_json text, reference text, implied_outcome text',\n    'evidence': 'evidence_id text primary key, quote text, one_line text, speaker text, original_who text, original_day text, tier text, event_time text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text',\n    'evidence_sources': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, evidence_id text, input_id text, category text, publication_day text, location text, seq integer',\n    'evidence_links': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, evidence_id text, view_id text, seq integer',\n    'replacements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer',   # history: written before D202, read as before\n    'revisions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, said_day text, seq integer',      # D202: the new piece revises the old; both stay in force\n    'same_claims': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, old_evidence_id text, new_evidence_id text, seq integer',                    # D204: the matcher read the new piece as the same claim as the old; both stored, both in force\n    'dependencies': 'dependency_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, depends_on text, wait_chain_view_id text, wait_year text, direction text, seq integer, kind text default \\'\\'',   # kind: '' (a seed's or the generative matcher's row, read as before) or 'reads' (a chosen reading link, D694)\n    'dependency_resolutions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, dependency_id integer, resolved_to text, reason text, seq integer',\n    'successions': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, succeeds text, seq integer',\n    'handovers': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, seq integer, handover_json text',\n    'match_records': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, seq integer, input_id text, call_no integer, shown_json text, request_sha256 text, call_id integer, decisions_json text, checks_json text, written_json text',\n    'processing_steps': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, sequence_no integer, step text, result text, reason text, publication_day text, at text',\n    'review_pool_entries': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, kind text, key text, example_json text, seq integer',\n    'late_statements': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, input_id text, evidence_quote text, reason text, seq integer',\n    'days_completed': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, day text, seq integer, at text',\n    # D694: how the links of an article were chosen (views/links.py), append-only per attempt: proposed, then committed or failed\n    'link_selections': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, attempt_id text, seq integer, input_id text, config_checksum text, status text, record_json text',\n    # D149 research groups: an ongoing business subject several distinct theses belong to; membership is decided by extraction and written with the thesis\n    'thesis_groups': 'group_id text primary key, name text, scope text, aliases text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text',\n    'thesis_group_members': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, view_id text, seq integer, input_id text, basis text',\n    # D166 (2026-11-01): the names a later declaration gives a stored group, appended once each; a group's aliases are its creation's plus these\n    'thesis_group_aliases': 'id integer primary key autoincrement, group_id text, alias text, seq integer, input_id text',\n}\n\nINDEXES = [\n    'create index if not exists views_object on views(object_id)',\n    'create index if not exists judgements_view on judgements(view_id, judgement_id)',\n    # 06-views step 7: a view is judged once per round (one item = one sequence number)\n    'create unique index if not exists judgements_once_per_round on judgements(view_id, seq)',\n    'create index if not exists links_view on evidence_links(view_id)',\n    'create index if not exists links_evidence on evidence_links(evidence_id)',\n    'create index if not exists sources_evidence on evidence_sources(evidence_id)',\n    'create index if not exists steps_input on processing_steps(input_id, id)',\n    'create index if not exists switches_view on view_switches(view_id, id)',\n    'create index if not exists deps_view on dependencies(view_id)',\n]\n\n\ndef open_db(path):\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    for name, columns in TABLES.items():\n        conn.execute(f'create table if not exists {name} ({columns})')\n        conn.execute(f\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_update before update on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\")\n        conn.execute(f\"create trigger if not exists {name}_no_delete before delete on {name} begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end\")\n    for statement in INDEXES:\n        conn.execute(statement)\n    ensure_writable_columns(conn)\n    conn.execute(\"create virtual table if not exists views_fts using fts5(view_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\")\n    conn.execute(\"create virtual table if not exists groups_fts using fts5(group_id unindexed, text, tokenize='trigram')\")\n    conn.execute('create index if not exists members_view on thesis_group_members(view_id)')\n    conn.commit()\n    return conn\n\n\ndef insert(conn, table, **fields):\n    columns = list(fields)\n    cursor = conn.execute(f'insert into {table} ({\",\".join(columns)}) values ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(columns))})', [fields[c] for c in columns])\n    return cursor.lastrowid\n\n\n# ---------- views ----------\n\ndef create_view(conn, *, view_id, object_id, object_kind, kind, looks_at, question, due_day, year, rungs, seq, input_id, created_at):\n    insert(conn, 'views', view_id=view_id, object_id=object_id, object_kind=object_kind, kind=kind, looks_at=looks_at,\n           question=question, due_day=due_day, year=year, created_seq=seq, created_from_input=input_id, created_at=created_at)\n    for position, rung in enumerate(rungs, start=1):\n        insert(conn, 'rungs', view_id=view_id, position=position, label=rung['label'], condition=rung['condition'], lo=rung.get('lo'), hi=rung.get('hi'))\n    insert(conn, 'view_switches', view_id=view_id, open=1, reason='created', by_whom='matching', after_seq=seq)\n    conn.execute('insert into views_fts (view_id, text) values (?, ?)', (view_id, f'{object_id} {looks_at} {question}'))\n\n\ndef view(conn, view_id):\n    row = conn.execute('select * from views where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n    return dict(row) if row else None\n\n\ndef rungs_of(conn, view_id):\n    \"\"\"The rungs with their bounds when the ledger has them (keyed views); a ledger written before keys has no lo/hi columns.\"\"\"\n    rows = [dict(r) for r in conn.execute('select * from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,))]\n    has_bounds = any(r.get('lo') is not None or r.get('hi') is not None for r in rows) or view_key(conn, view_id) is not None\n    return [dict(position=r['position'], label=r['label'], condition=r['condition'],\n                 **({'lo': r.get('lo'), 'hi': r.get('hi')} if has_bounds else {})) for r in rows]\n\n\ndef add_key(conn, view_id, key, seq):\n    \"\"\"The view's key (keyed-views-plan.md 2.1), written once with the view.\"\"\"\n    from .. import universe as _universe\n    from .identity import is_shared\n    scope_source = 'shared' if is_shared(key) else key.get('scope_source', 'model')      # D197: an aggregate's scope is wording\n    insert(conn, 'view_keys', view_id=view_id, measure=key['measure'], scope=key.get('scope', ''), scope_key=_universe.scope_key(key.get('scope', '')),\n**Not ready to build.** Revision 5 closes both 74d defects at `--out`. Two issues remain. Test 14 checks the command’s exit status on the wrong path, and cleanup can delete a directory that reuses the staging name after publication.\n\n1. **Both 74d defects are closed in the design.** The only operation that creates `--out` is an atomic move that refuses an existing destination, including an empty directory. A database error before that move leaves only private staging to clean up. Test 17 specifies the missing-table error, exit 1, absence of both output and staging, and a successful retry at the same path. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:142) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:171](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:171) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:329](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:329)\n\n2. **Test 14 still misses the command’s late refusal.** Its module test creates the foreign empty directory after staging. Its command test creates the directory before startup, so the early check can return exit 1 without ever reaching `publish` or staging cleanup. Run the real command on a scratch copy with a pause immediately before `publish`, create the empty directory, then resume. Assert exit 1, removal of the build’s staging folder, and survival of the same empty directory by device and inode. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:161](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:161) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:212) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:326](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:326) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:328](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:328)\n\n3. **Revision 5 introduces a cleanup race at the old staging name.** Once `publish` succeeds, the rename frees that name. If another process creates a directory there before `finally` runs, the specified “if it still exists” check can remove the new directory. End the build’s cleanup responsibility as soon as the move succeeds. The decisive test recreates the old staging directory with a marker file after the move and verifies that the marker survives command exit. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:138](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:138) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:163](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:163) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:167)**Not ready to build.** Revision 6 closes both 74e findings. Two other issues remain. A package dated August 25 can include September evidence, and writing the report can overwrite an input database.\n\n**1. Both 74e findings are closed in the design.**\n\n- **Late refusal.** Test 14 now pauses the real command immediately before `publish`, creates an empty `--out`, and resumes. It requires exit 1, removal of this build’s staging folder, and survival of the same empty directory, verified by device and inode. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:336](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:336)\n- **Cleanup after publication.** The builder clears its staging path immediately after the move succeeds. Test 14 recreates the freed name with a marker file and requires the marker to survive command exit. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:339](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:339)\n\n**2. Two findings block the build.**\n\n- **The date must be normalized before comparison.** Python accepts `20260825` and `2026-08-25` as the same day. The design passes the original text to `resolve_bound`, and evidence visibility also compares dates as text. I reproduced the consequence on an in-memory copy of `old-1`, adding only a completed day in January 2027. For `v8`, `2026-08-25` returned 621 evidence records through August 25. `20260825` returned 1,284 through September 20. Parse an explicit date before calling `resolve_bound`, use its `YYYY-MM-DD` form for every query, and require that form in the package. Test that both command-line spellings produce the same evidence. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:95) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:121](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:121) · [service.py:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:69) · [service.py:113](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:113)\n- **The report can replace the ledger or items database.** For example, with `--out /work/release` and a valid SQLite input named `/work/release.report.json`, the build can read the input, verify and publish the package, then replace that database with JSON. The standalone `check` command rewrites the same path. Both commands should refuse a report destination that resolves to either input before writing anything. The decisive test is that each command refuses the collision and the input’s bytes remain intact. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:166](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:166) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:175) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:185](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:185)**Not ready to build.** Revision 7 closes the date finding. Two ways to overwrite a file remain in the report-writing steps.\n\n1. **74f date finding — closed.** The builder rejects `20260825` before querying the ledger. The package checker also requires `YYYY-MM-DD`. Test 16 places evidence on both sides of August 25 and checks that the canonical date exports only the earlier evidence. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:100](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:100) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:116](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:116) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:359](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:359)\n\n2. **74f input-overwrite finding — still open in `check`.** On this Mac, I verified read-only that `old-1/prod/views.sqlite` and `old-1/prod/VIEWS.SQLITE` produce different `realpath` strings and identify the same file. An items database named `Release.report.json` can therefore pass the path comparison for `check release`, which then rewrites `release.report.json`. Compare the existing report’s file identity with both inputs using `os.path.samefile`. Extend test 18 on a case-insensitive volume to require refusal and an unchanged database hash. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:192) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:351](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:351) · [live_lock.py:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:40)\n\n3. **Additional blocker — `build` can overwrite a file created while it runs.** The builder checks that the report name is free at startup. If another process creates a file there while the package is being checked, the final `os.replace` overwrites it. Publish the build’s report with an atomic operation that refuses an occupied destination. The decisive test places a marker file there immediately before the report write and requires the marker to survive, the checked package to remain available, and the command to exit 2. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:182](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:182) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:188](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:188)\n\nI found no further serious blocker in slice 1.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,pathlib\npaths=sorted(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\").glob(\\\"old-*/prod/views.sqlite\\\"))+list(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data\\\").glob(\\\"served-*/views.sqlite\\\"))\nfor i,p in enumerate(paths):\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?immutable=1&mode=ro\\\",uri=True)\n if i in (0,2):\n  v,d=((\\\"v10\\\",\\\"2026-08-28\\\") if i==0 else (\\\"v36\\\",\\\"2026-08-25\\\"))\n  print(i, c.execute(\\\"select view_id,judgement_id,publication_day from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1\\\",(v,d)).fetchone())\n print(p,c.execute(\\\"select count(*) from (select view_id,evidence_id from evidence_links group by 1,2 having count(*)>1)\\\").fetchone())\n if i==0:\n  print(list(c.execute(\\\"select view_id,evidence_id from evidence_links where evidence_id in (?,?,?)\\\",(\\\"e1865\\\",\\\"e2295\\\",\\\"e3597\\\"))))\n  print(list(c.execute(\\\"select old_evidence_id from replacements where old_evidence_id in (?,?,?)\\\",(\\\"e1865\\\",\\\"e2295\\\",\\\"e3597\\\"))))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,pathlib\npaths=sorted(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\").glob(\\\"old-*/prod/views.sqlite\\\"))+list(pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data\\\").glob(\\\"served-*/views.sqlite\\\"))\nfor i,p in enumerate(paths):\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?immutable=1&mode=ro\\\",uri=True)\n if i in (0,2):\n  v,d=((\\\"v10\\\",\\\"2026-08-28\\\") if i==0 else (\\\"v36\\\",\\\"2026-08-25\\\"))\n  print(i, c.execute(\\\"select view_id,judgement_id,publication_day from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1\\\",(v,d)).fetchone())\n print(p,c.execute(\\\"select count(*) from (select view_id,evidence_id from evidence_links group by 1,2 having count(*)>1)\\\").fetchone())\n if i==0:\n  print(list(c.execute(\\\"select view_id,evidence_id from evidence_links where evidence_id in (?,?,?)\\\",(\\\"e1865\\\",\\\"e2295\\\",\\\"e3597\\\"))))\n  print(list(c.execute(\\\"select old_evidence_id from replacements where old_evidence_id in (?,?,?)\\\",(\\\"e1865\\\",\\\"e2295\\\",\\\"e3597\\\"))))'\"","aggregated_output":"0 ('v10', 865, '2026-08-28')\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite (0,)\n[('v4', 'e1865'), ('v5', 'e1865'), ('v8', 'e1865'), ('v8', 'e2295'), ('v4', 'e3597'), ('v5', 'e3597')]\n[]\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite (0,)\n2 ('v36', 799, '2026-08-25')\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite (0,)\npoc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite (0,)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
